<title>FRANCE: Usinor est 96 net profit 1.49 bln Ffr.</title>
<headline>Usinor est 96 net profit 1.49 bln Ffr.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Twelve months to Dec 31, 1996.</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of French francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net attributable profit		  1,489  vs	   4,430</p>
<p>    Turnover				    71,059  vs	  78,423</p>
<p>    Net debt				     6,538  down  4,506 from</p>
<p>end 1995</p>
<p>    Debt to equity ratio		  0.22 pct  vs	0.38 pct</p>
<p>    Net dividend (francs)		     3.0   vs	   4.0</p>
<p>Rounded off results from company in billions of francs:</p>
<p>    Pre-tax, pre-exceptional profit	2.1    vs	   6.1</p>
<p>    Operating				    2.5    vs	   8.0</p>
<p>    Cashflow				     5.5    vs	   8.1</p>
<p>    Shareholders equity			29.7   vs	  28.9</p>
<p>NOTE - In a statement the group said that while volumes are showing significant growth, average prices should, at least for the first half, be lower than in 1996.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
